<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Dneper II Unloading   rapeseed	 668     Europe</p>
<p>				     feed wheat	  643</p>
<p>				     sunflower	   664</p>
<p>Valday	     Arrived     barley	    2,800     Europe</p>
<p>Sormovsky 17     Arrived     feed wheat	2,860     Europe</p>
<p>Mete Arrived     barleu	    2,508     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 237	4/11	 sunflower meal  2,000     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Wave	5/11	 corn	     32,450     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   9,072</p>
<p>				     wheat	    19,306</p>
<p>Sormovsky 10	5/11	 barley	    2,853     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	10/11	 soya	     26,500     U.S.</p>
</text>
